--- LST-43, LST-45: insert and replace, same map ---
a map called cupboard is {"the contents": 947}.
Set cupboard's "the contents" to 171.
a number called 'cupboard replaced value seen' is cupboard's "the contents".
If 'cupboard replaced value seen' is not 171 then, Print "ASSERT LST-45: expected 171 got {'cupboard replaced value seen'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard replaced value seen'.
If cupboard's length is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-45: expected 1 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
Set cupboard's "the reply" to 702.
a number called 'cupboard inserted value seen' is cupboard's "the reply".
If 'cupboard inserted value seen' is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST-43: expected 702 got {'cupboard inserted value seen'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard inserted value seen'.
If cupboard's length is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT LST-43: expected 2 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a map called cupboard is {"the contents": 947},
  Set cupboard's "the contents" to 171,
  a number called 'cupboard replaced value seen' is cupboard's "the contents",
  If 'cupboard replaced value seen' is not 171 then, Print "ASSERT LST-45: expected 171 got {'cupboard replaced value seen'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard replaced value seen',
  If cupboard's length is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-45: expected 1 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  Set cupboard's "the reply" to 702,
  a number called 'cupboard inserted value seen' is cupboard's "the reply",
  If 'cupboard inserted value seen' is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST-43: expected 702 got {'cupboard inserted value seen'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard inserted value seen',
  If cupboard's length is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT LST-43: expected 2 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.

--- LST-46: length and empty, an empty map and a populated one ---
a map called cupboard is {}.
If cupboard's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 0 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
If cupboard's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 1 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty.
a map called 'workbench' is {"numeral": 702, "the receipt": 494, "the slot": 83}.
If 'workbench's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 3 got {'workbench's length}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's length.
If 'workbench's empty then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 0 got {'workbench's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's empty.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a map called cupboard is {},
  If cupboard's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 0 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  If cupboard's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 1 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty,
  a map called 'workbench' is {"numeral": 702, "the receipt": 494, "the slot": 83},
  If 'workbench's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 3 got {'workbench's length}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's length,
  If 'workbench's empty then, Print "ASSERT LST-46: expected 0 got {'workbench's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's empty.

--- LST-04: an empty list, length 0 and empty true before any append ---
a list called cupboard is [].
If cupboard's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-04: expected 0 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
If cupboard's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT LST-04: expected 1 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [],
  If cupboard's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-04: expected 0 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  If cupboard's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT LST-04: expected 1 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty.

--- LST-47: keys/values order and freshness, a two-key map ---
a map called cupboard is {"the reply": 947, "numeral": 702}.
a list called 'satchel' is cupboard's keys.
a list called ledger is cupboard's values.
If element 1 of 'satchel' is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of 'satchel'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'satchel'.
If element 2 of 'satchel' is not "numeral" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected numeral got {element 2 of 'satchel'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'satchel'.
If element 1 of ledger is not 947 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 947 got {element 1 of ledger}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of ledger.
If element 2 of ledger is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 702 got {element 2 of ledger}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of ledger.
Set element 1 of 'satchel' to "mutated".
If cupboard's length is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 2 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
a list called notebook is cupboard's keys.
If element 1 of notebook is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of notebook}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of notebook.
Set cupboard's "the reply" to 368.
a list called 'the tally sheet' is cupboard's keys.
If element 1 of 'the tally sheet' is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of 'the tally sheet'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the tally sheet'.
Set cupboard's "the tin" to 646.
a list called 'the waybill' is cupboard's keys.
If element 3 of 'the waybill' is not "the tin" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the tin got {element 3 of 'the waybill'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'the waybill'.
Print cupboard's length.

--- the same leaf, a three-key map ---
a map called pantry is {"freight": 992, "the token": 977}.
a list called 'the tally sheet' is pantry's keys.
a list called 'the sketchpad' is pantry's values.
If element 1 of 'the tally sheet' is not "freight" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected freight got {element 1 of 'the tally sheet'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the tally sheet'.
If element 2 of 'the tally sheet' is not "the token" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the token got {element 2 of 'the tally sheet'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'the tally sheet'.
If element 1 of 'the sketchpad' is not 992 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 992 got {element 1 of 'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the sketchpad'.
If element 2 of 'the sketchpad' is not 977 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 977 got {element 2 of 'the sketchpad'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'the sketchpad'.
Set element 1 of 'the tally sheet' to "mutated".
If pantry's length is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 2 got {pantry's length}", Exit 95. Print pantry's length.
a list called 'the waybill' is pantry's keys.
If element 1 of 'the waybill' is not "freight" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected freight got {element 1 of 'the waybill'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the waybill'.
Set pantry's "freight" to 789.
a list called 'the inbox' is pantry's keys.
If element 1 of 'the inbox' is not "freight" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected freight got {element 1 of 'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the inbox'.
Set pantry's "the delivery" to 721.
a list called 'the register' is pantry's keys.
If element 3 of 'the register' is not "the delivery" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the delivery got {element 3 of 'the register'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'the register'.
Print pantry's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a map called cupboard is {"the reply": 947, "numeral": 702},
  a list called 'satchel' is cupboard's keys,
  a list called ledger is cupboard's values,
  If element 1 of 'satchel' is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of 'satchel'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'satchel',
  If element 2 of 'satchel' is not "numeral" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected numeral got {element 2 of 'satchel'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'satchel',
  If element 1 of ledger is not 947 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 947 got {element 1 of ledger}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of ledger,
  If element 2 of ledger is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 702 got {element 2 of ledger}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of ledger,
  Set element 1 of 'satchel' to "mutated",
  If cupboard's length is not 2 then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected 2 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  a list called notebook is cupboard's keys,
  If element 1 of notebook is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of notebook}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of notebook,
  Set cupboard's "the reply" to 368,
  a list called 'the tally sheet' is cupboard's keys,
  If element 1 of 'the tally sheet' is not "the reply" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the reply got {element 1 of 'the tally sheet'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the tally sheet',
  Set cupboard's "the tin" to 646,
  a list called 'the waybill' is cupboard's keys,
  If element 3 of 'the waybill' is not "the tin" then, Print "ASSERT LST-47: expected the tin got {element 3 of 'the waybill'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'the waybill',
  Print cupboard's length.

--- LST-49: a missing key, the provable and the Set-grown/typed-default halves ---
a map called whatever is {"the handout": 308}.
a boolean called payload is false.
On error Set payload to true.
a number called 'what arrived' is 0.
a number called 'the answer' is whatever's "no such entry".
On error Set 'what arrived' to 1.
If 'what arrived' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the provable missing read to raise the error flag got 'what arrived'", Exit 95.
If 'the answer' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the provable missing read to be 0 got 'the answer'", Exit 95.
a map called 'the cargo' is {}.
Set 'the cargo's "the reply" to 171.
a number called 'the reading' is 0.
a text called cargo is 'the cargo's "leftover".
On error Set 'the reading' to 1.
If 'the reading' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the text-typed missing read to raise the error flag got 'the reading'", Exit 95.
a buffer called 'the tally' is cargo.
If 'the tally's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-text default to be 0 bytes got 'the tally's size", Exit 95.
a number called token is 0.
a list called 'the token' is 'the cargo's "leftover".
On error Set token to 1.
If token is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the list-typed missing read to raise the error flag got token", Exit 95.
If 'the token's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-list default to have length 0 got 'the token's length", Exit 95.
a number called 'the label' is 0.
a map called 'the slot' is 'the cargo's "leftover".
On error Set 'the label' to 1.
If 'the label' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the map-typed missing read to raise the error flag got 'the label'", Exit 95.
If 'the slot's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-map default to have length 0 got 'the slot's length", Exit 95.
Print 'the slot'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a map called 'what came back' is {"the handout": 308}.
  a boolean called numeral is false.
  On error Set numeral to true.
  a number called 'the guess' is 0.
  a number called 'the numeral' is 'what came back's "no such entry".
  On error Set 'the guess' to 1.
  If 'the guess' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the provable missing read to raise the error flag got 'the guess'", Exit 95.
  If 'the numeral' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the provable missing read to be 0 got 'the numeral'", Exit 95.
  a map called guess is {}.
  Set guess's "the reply" to 171.
  a number called offering is 0.
  a text called 'the offering' is guess's "leftover".
  On error Set offering to 1.
  If offering is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the text-typed missing read to raise the error flag got offering", Exit 95.
  a buffer called 'the receipt' is 'the offering'.
  If 'the receipt's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-text default to be 0 bytes got 'the receipt's size", Exit 95.
  a number called 'the sample' is 0.
  a list called receipt is guess's "leftover".
  On error Set 'the sample' to 1.
  If 'the sample' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the list-typed missing read to raise the error flag got 'the sample'", Exit 95.
  If receipt's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-list default to have length 0 got receipt's length", Exit 95.
  a number called 'the shipment' is 0.
  a map called sample is guess's "leftover".
  On error Set 'the shipment' to 1.
  If 'the shipment' is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the map-typed missing read to raise the error flag got 'the shipment'", Exit 95.
  If sample's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST-49: expected the empty-map default to have length 0 got sample's length", Exit 95.
  Print sample.

--- LST2-30: two appends onto a populated list, length +2 ---
a list called cupboard is [534, 947].
append 171 to cupboard.
append 702 to cupboard.
If cupboard's length is not 4 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-30: expected 4 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
If element 4 of cupboard is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-30: expected 702 got {element 4 of cupboard}", Exit 95. Print element 4 of cupboard.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [534, 947],
  append 171 to cupboard,
  append 702 to cupboard,
  If cupboard's length is not 4 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-30: expected 4 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  If element 4 of cupboard is not 702 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-30: expected 702 got {element 4 of cupboard}", Exit 95. Print element 4 of cupboard.

--- LST2-41: append inside a While loop, a drawn bound ---
a list called cupboard is [].
a number called 'cupboard running count' is 1.
While 'cupboard running count' is less than or equal to 3, append 'cupboard running count' multiply 'cupboard running count' to cupboard, increment 'cupboard running count'.
If cupboard's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-41: expected 3 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
If element 3 of cupboard is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-41: expected 9 got {element 3 of cupboard}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of cupboard.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [],
  a number called 'cupboard running count' is 1,
  While 'cupboard running count' is less than or equal to 3, append 'cupboard running count' multiply 'cupboard running count' to cupboard, increment 'cupboard running count',
  If cupboard's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-41: expected 3 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  If element 3 of cupboard is not 9 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-41: expected 9 got {element 3 of cupboard}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of cupboard.

--- LST2-46, LST2-53: append each X from Y to Z, element by element ---
a list called cupboard is [226, 494, 124].
a list called 'workbench' is [].
append each storeroom from cupboard to 'workbench'.
If 'workbench's length is not cupboard's length then, Print "ASSERT LST2-46: expected {cupboard's length} got {'workbench's length}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's length.
If element 1 of 'workbench' is not 226 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 226 got {element 1 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'workbench'.
If element 2 of 'workbench' is not 494 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 494 got {element 2 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'workbench'.
If element 3 of 'workbench' is not 124 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 124 got {element 3 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'workbench'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [226, 494, 124],
  a list called 'workbench' is [],
  append each storeroom from cupboard to 'workbench',
  If 'workbench's length is not cupboard's length then, Print "ASSERT LST2-46: expected {cupboard's length} got {'workbench's length}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench's length,
  If element 1 of 'workbench' is not 226 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 226 got {element 1 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'workbench',
  If element 2 of 'workbench' is not 494 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 494 got {element 2 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'workbench',
  If element 3 of 'workbench' is not 124 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-53: expected 124 got {element 3 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'workbench'.

--- LST2-94: a treating clause with a guaranteed hit ---
a list called cupboard is [49, 38, 27, 36].
a list called 'workbench' is [].
append each storeroom from cupboard treating 49 as 112 to 'workbench'.
If element 1 of 'workbench' is not 112 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 112 got {element 1 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'workbench'.
If element 2 of 'workbench' is not 38 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 38 got {element 2 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'workbench'.
If element 3 of 'workbench' is not 27 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 27 got {element 3 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'workbench'.
If element 4 of 'workbench' is not 36 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 36 got {element 4 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 4 of 'workbench'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [49, 38, 27, 36],
  a list called 'workbench' is [],
  append each storeroom from cupboard treating 49 as 112 to 'workbench',
  If element 1 of 'workbench' is not 112 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 112 got {element 1 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'workbench',
  If element 2 of 'workbench' is not 38 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 38 got {element 2 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 2 of 'workbench',
  If element 3 of 'workbench' is not 27 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 27 got {element 3 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'workbench',
  If element 4 of 'workbench' is not 36 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-94: expected 36 got {element 4 of 'workbench'}", Exit 95. Print element 4 of 'workbench'.

